slhdsa — provenance note
========================

This file carries NO condition. It exists because the module reproduces
third-party test data verbatim and the repository's rule (root `NOTICE` §0) is
that reproduced data is recorded where it lives — even when, as here, the
record turns out to owe nothing.

Until 2026-09-09 this module had no NOTICE at all, while `src/kat_vectors.zig`
carried NIST's vectors for all twelve SLH-DSA parameter sets. The provenance
was written in that file's own doc comment, which is the right place for it,
but a reader asking "what does this module owe?" had nothing to open.

Test vectors
------------

`src/kat_vectors.zig` reproduces the official NIST ACVP known-answer vectors
for FIPS 205 (SLH-DSA), retrieved 2026-07-11 from
`github.com/usnistgov/ACVP-Server`:

  - `gen-val/json-files/SLH-DSA-keyGen-FIPS205/internalProjection.json`
  - `gen-val/json-files/SLH-DSA-sigGen-FIPS205/internalProjection.json`

The hex is copied verbatim (lowercased) out of that JSON; each entry's own
doc comment names its exact `tgId`/`tcId`, so any value here can be traced to
one upstream case. Per parameter set: one keyGen case and one sigGen case
(internal interface, deterministic); SLH-DSA-SHA2-128f additionally carries a
pure external deterministic case with a 110-byte context and a hedged internal
case.

